        These are the cases where, on the boundary, precisely one variable vanishes. The discussion for these three cases is presented below.


     \textbf{\text{Case 3:} One variable approaches zero}

        \begin{itemize}
            \item $ x \to 0, y \to \bar{y} \geq \bar{\delta}, z \to \bar{z} \geq \bar{\delta} $
