%Such a view considers the GroEL/GroES cavity as a passive anti-aggregation device~\cite{Horwich09FEBSLett,Hoffmann10PNAS}. 
%On the other hand, it has been suggested by a number of single molecule measurements that 
%ATP-binding and hydrolysis induced large-scale conformational adaptation of GroEL exert mechanical stress to the encapsulated proteins, which destabilizes misfolded proteins~\cite{korobko2022diminished,koculi2021retardation,korobko2020Elife}. 
%This view puts GroEL into a perspective of molecular nanomachine that exerts mechanical force on the substrate proteins.   
%Regardless of the detailed mechanism, the net consequence of the chaperonin action of GroEL on the population of misfolding-prone proteins is that the yield of native state increases over time. 

