We know  the symmetric coinvariant divisors associated to representations in $\mathcal{S}_2(k)$ for levels $k \leq 5$ are nef.  It is natural to ask whether these divisors are base-point free, and if so, what morphisms they define? Since the intersection numbers of these divisors with $F$-curves satisfy a modularity condition that is truly distinct from those arising in  \cite{Veronese, Noah, NoahAngela} — one should expect something entirely new.
