\section{Introduction}
\label{Introduction}

Horowitz {\it et al.} \cite{PRC.63.025501} proposed a direct measurement for neutron skin thickness $r_{\rm skin}$ = $r_{\rm n} - r_{\rm p}$, where 
$r_{\rm n}$ ($r_{\rm p}$) is the root-mean-square radii of neutrons 
(protons). 

The PREX collaboration reported~\cite{Adhikari:2021phr} 
\begin{equation}
r^{208Pb}_{skin}({\rm PREX\text{-}II}) 
= 0.283\pm 0.071\,{\rm fm}.
\label{Eq:Experimental constraint 208}
\end{equation}
The CREX group also did~\cite{CREX:2022kgg} 
\bea
&&r_{\rm skin}^{48Ca}({\rm CREX}) \nonumber \\
&&=0.121 \pm 0.026\ {\rm (exp)} \pm 0.024\ {\rm (model)}\,{\rm fm}. 
 \label{CREX-value}
 \eea

The values of   matter radii $r_{\rm m}({\rm exp})$, neutron radii $r_{\rm n}({\rm exp})$, 
$r_{\rm skin}({\rm exp})$, $r_{\rm p}({\rm exp})$ are tabulated in Table \ref{TW-prex} 
for $^{208}$Pb and $^{48}$Ca. 




