Using the precise data for  $^{12}$C+$^{12}$C scattering, 
we tested the Kyushu $g$-matrix folding model for  $^{12}$C+$^{12}$C scattering, and found that the model is reliable for 
$\sigma_{\rm R}$
in $30  \lsim E_{\rm lab} \lsim 100 $~MeV/u and $250  \lsim E_{\rm lab} \lsim 400 $~MeV/u~\cite{PRC.101.014620}. Note that no data is available in $ E_{\rm lab} \leq 30$~MeV/u.  


