We extract  $r_{\rm skin}$ and $r_{\rm m}(\sigma_{\rm R})$ from  the data $\sigma_{\rm R}$~\cite{ABEGG1979109}  in $20  \leq E_{\rm lab} \leq 47.5$~MeV, using the Kyushu $g$-matrix folding model with the  D1S-GHFB densities.  $^{159}$Tb is a deformed nucleus;
the deformation parameter $\b_2$ 
calculated with D1S-GHFB is 0.309.


Figure \ref{Fig-Xsec-p+Tb} shows our  $\sigma_{\rm R}$  based on the Kyushu $g$-matrix folding model with the  D1S-GHFB densities and  the data~\cite{ABEGG1979109}. 
