Taking the scaling procedure of Sec.~\ref{Scaling procedure} for the D1S-GHFB proton and neutron densities, i.e., 
 for each $E_{\rm lab}$, we scale $r_{\rm n}(E_{\rm lab})$ so as to  $\sigma_{\rm R}({\rm scaled})=\sigma_{\rm R}({\rm exp})$
under $r_{\rm p,scaled}=r_{\rm p}({\rm exp})$ of electron scattering~\cite{Angeli:2013epw}. 
We next take a weighted average of  $r_{\rm n}(E_{\rm lab})$ over $E_{\rm lab}$. 
