% for some measure $\sigma(z)dz$. Call $D$ the set of all such functions: this is an equivalent representation of the cone $G(\vec{t})$. Similarly, call $\tilde{D}$ the cone of all functions $y$ such that the matrix $(y(k-j):j,k=1,...,N)$ is positive semidefinite. Obviously, $\tilde{D}$ is another representation of $\tilde{G}(\vec{t})$.

