\[{(P_{L}AP_{L})}^{2k+1} y=\tilde{A} x=0.\]
Hence, we have $y\in\mathcal{N}({(P_{L}AP_{L})}^{2 k+1})=T$
which means $x=(P_{L}AP_{L})^{k} y=0$.
On the other hand, for every $y\in{S}$ there exists an $x\in\mathbb{C}^{n}$ such that
