$z_{2}\in S$. It follows that there exists a
$t\in\mathbb{C}^{n}$ such that $z_{2}=(P_{L}AP_{L})^{k+1}t$ since $S=\mathcal{R}((P_{L}AP_{L})^{k+1})$.
Finally, we can verify that  $X=\tilde{A}^{-1}{(P_{L}AP_{L})}^{k}$ satisfies the three equations in $(\ref{dra})$.
