\section{Conclusion}
In this work. Our main goal is to present a new generalized inverse, that is, BDD-inverse,
which extends the notion of the Bott-Duffin inverse.
Note that the inverse exists for any square matrix.
We show some of its properties, characterizations and representations.
Furthermore, the BDD-inverse can be used in solving appropriate systems of constrained matrix equations.
The minimum P-norm solution of the corresponding constraint equation is given by applying the BDD-inverse.
Finally, we discussed Cramer's rule for the minimum P-norm solution of constraint equation.
However, based on current research, there are many topics that can be discussed in the BDD-inverse. Some ideas for further research are given below:
\vspace{0.2cm}
\par${(a)}$ The relationship between BDD-inverse and other generalized inverses.
\par${(b)}$ Continuity and perturbation of the BDG-inverse, and the use of iterative methods to calculate the BDG-inverse.
