\subsection{Visualization of Entropy $\mathcal{H}(d)$ and CoG State Dimension Selection}
\label{subsecapp:entropy-vis}
Fig.~\ref{fig:SMAC-entropy} and Fig.~\ref{fig:GRF-entropy} visualize \( \mathcal{H}(d) \) for SMAC and GRF. To facilitate comparison, \( \mathcal{H}(d) \) values are min-max normalized to the range \([0, 1]\) within each environment. In GRF, \(\mathrm{CoG}_\delta\) consistently highlights goalkeeper positions, which are critical for evaluating offensive positioning and shot opportunities, as discussed in Appendix~\ref{secapp:grf-strategy-analysis}. In SMAC, it emphasizes enemy health, a key factor for prioritizing targets and coordinating attacks. These results indicate that SFI effectively identifies state dimensions essential for solving the underlying tasks. Although ally-specific features such as unit type, which only change when an agent is eliminated by enemy, are included in the CoG dimensions, FIM emphasizes features that allies can directly influence and thus prioritizes enemy health and shield to increase influence eligibility traces.


