\label{secapp:grf-strategy-analysis}
\begin{figure}[!h]
  \centering
  \includegraphics[width=1\linewidth]{fig/GRF-analysis.pdf}
  \caption{FIM trajectory in GRF \texttt{academy\_3\_vs\_2\_full\_field}}
  \label{fig:GRF-analysis}
\end{figure}

In GRF, the CoG state dimensions identified by FIM primarily correspond to the position of the opponent goalkeeper, as illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:GRF-analysis}(a). These dimensions exhibit low entropy under random behavior, since the goalkeeper typically remains stationary and only shifts position when a ball-carrying agent approaches the goalpost. This characteristic makes the goalkeeper’s state both stable and strategically significant, as displacing it creates scoring opportunities and thus serves as a valuable proxy objective in sparse reward settings. Accordingly, FIM guides agents to influence the goalkeeper’s position, as it aligns closely with the task objective.

% In GRF 환경에서 FIM이 식별한 CoG 상태 차원은 주로 상대 골키퍼의 위치에 해당하며, 이는 Fig.~\ref{fig:GRF-analysis}(a)에 시각화되어 있다. 이러한 차원은 무작위 행동 하에서 낮은 엔트로피를 보이는데, 이는 골키퍼가 일반적으로 정지 상태를 유지하다가 공을 소유한 에이전트가 골문 근처에 접근할 때만 위치를 변경하기 때문이다. 이러한 특성으로 인해 골키퍼의 상태는 안정적이면서도 전략적으로 중요한 요소가 되며, 이를 변화시키는 것은 득점 기회를 창출하므로 희소 보상 환경에서 유용한 프록시 목표가 된다. 이에 따라 FIM은 골키퍼의 위치에 영향을 미치는 방향으로 에이전트의 행동을 유도하며, 이는 주어진 과업 목표와 밀접하게 정렬된다.


As shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:GRF-analysis}(b)-(c), this insight is reflected in the agent trajectory. Around $t \approx 70$, agents begin to receive intrinsic rewards by subtly influencing the goalkeeper’s position, even while positioned far from the goal area. By $t \approx 100$, the accumulated eligibility traces further incentivize agents to continue exerting influence over the goalkeeper, enabling a gradual progression toward the goal. Near $t \approx 130$, the goalkeeper briefly moves out of position, and the attacking agent capitalizes on this opportunity to score. Notably, FIM guides agents to approach the goal proactively and maintain persistent influence over the goalkeeper’s positioning, which serves as a task critical factor for successful coordination in this environment, particularly under sparse reward conditions.

