    \begin{example}[Triangle inequality failure] \label{example:tri_ineq}
        Let $\Gamma = \Z/10\Z * \Z/10\Z = \la a,b \,|\, a^{10} = b^{10} \ra$, and let $X$ be the Cayley graph for $\Gamma$ with respect to the generating set above. Then the function $\rho:\p X \times \p X \rightarrow [0,\infty)$ given by $\rho(\eta,\eta') = e^{-(\eta,\eta')_p}$ does not satisfy the triangle inequality. Indeed, let $\eta, \eta', \eta''$ be three points in $\p X$ as shown in \Cref{figure-tri_inequality}.

