polyseries, Catalan numbers, modular polynomial resolution}

\begin{abstract}
We study the computational framework of \emph{polyseries} and \emph{%
poly numbers} introduced by Wildberger and Rubine in \cite%
{wildberger2025hyper}. After reviewing Peano arithmetic, computable
naturals, and non-standard models, we define the core data and procedure
operations on polyseries. We then apply Catalan number expansions to solve
quadratic congruences

\begin{equation*}
t + a x + x^2 \equiv 0 \;\;(\mathrm{mod}\;t^n),
\end{equation*}

and derive explicit truncated series formulas in a finite field\thinspace\ $%
\mathbb{Z}_{p}$. Our main result gives a closed form poly series solution in
terms of Catalan numbers.
\end{abstract}

