up to degree $10.$ \ For more examples see \cite{wildberger2025hyper}

\section{\textbf{Conclusion}}

By the development of the modern constructive methods implemented in Category theory based on classical Data structures, we observe that Finistic perspectives in this field provide each time true equivalent statements such as the above main theorem \ref{ModPolyResoTheo}.  We have shown how Wildberger's polyseries framework, together with Catalan expansions, yields explicit truncated series solutions to quadratic congruences in finite fields. This method extends naturally to higher degree
equations via Fuss Catalan numbers and Hensel lifting techniques. They can be easily implemented using any automatic assistant prover.

