The distinct timescales of the two dissociation channels, as well as their distinct $Q$-dependent scattering, serve to drive the total integrated signal between $3.3$~\edit{$\mathrm{\AA}^{-1}$}$<Q<4.3$~$\mathrm{\AA}^{-1}$ lower as the reaction progresses.}


