\section{Questions}

% For every girth $g$ what is the smallest $d$, such that there exisits a $d$-regular graph of girth $g$ that is not a subgraph of a minimal Cayley Graph?
% Does every cubic graph of girth at least $4$ admit a no-lonely-color coloring?
% Is every connected cubic graph of girth $4$ subgraph of a minimal Cayley graph? 
Our work leaves two principal questions open:

\begin{conj}
For every integer $g\geq 3$ there is a connected cubic graph of girth $g$ that is not a subgraph of a minimal Cayley graph.
\end{conj}



\begin{conj}
Every generalized Petersen graph is an induced subgraph of a minimal Cayley graph.    
\end{conj}

